So this week we continue our re-watch of Avatar the Last Airbender

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.877
with Episode 3: The Southern Air Temple

00:00:09.877 --> 00:00:11.697
One of my favourite early Avatar episodes

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.560
Just because we get to see scary Aang, and Agni Kai

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:15.520
So here we go

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.574
If you're brand new here, we're re-watching all the Last Airbender episodes

00:00:18.574 --> 00:00:20.405
And I'm just doing a weekly Avatar giveaway

00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:21.915
Details at the end of the video

00:00:21.915 --> 00:00:25.885
Careful for spoilers; I know, it's silly to say that, but let's start with Top Five Moments

00:00:25.885 --> 00:00:28.119
Number 5: Team Aang, Family Car Trip

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:31.354
So now that they've gotten away from Zuko, safely, and the fire nation soldiers

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:34.647
Aang has gone full-blown Disneyland crazy

00:00:34.668 --> 00:00:36.828
It's like Sokka's the sleepy dad

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:41.490
who promised he'd take little kid Aang to Disneyland on his one weekend off from his ice-fishing job

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.570
All he cares about is getting another hour of sleep

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.180
But Aang just starts poking the hell out of him

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.300
In his sleeping bag

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.776
then Katara's like the mom, trying to calm him down

00:00:49.776 --> 00:00:52.416
"Maybe Disneyland won't be as awesome as you remembered it"

00:00:52.416 --> 00:00:55.680
"Just try not to drink too much Red Bull and Mountain Bull before we get there"

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.360
This plays out like almost every single family car trip I ever went on

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.951
except I have a little brother and a little sister

00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:05.120
So my scenario was more like after Toph and Zuko showed up

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.096
then it got a little more crowded on top of Appa

00:01:07.096 --> 00:01:10.294
And just to be clear, no, I never drank Mountain Dew and Red Bull as a child

00:01:10.426 --> 00:01:11.706
that's disgusting

00:01:12.184 --> 00:01:14.184
Number 4: Meet Commander Zhao

00:01:14.184 --> 00:01:17.135
I'd say out of all the last Airbender villains, Zhao's one of my favourites

00:01:17.135 --> 00:01:20.150
Him showing up makes Zuko start seeming more sympathetic

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.103
you know, not that it's clear from their first interaction here

00:01:23.103 --> 00:01:24.940
Zuko's still in super bro mode

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.778
But Zhao trying to shut him down immediately does make you forget that Zuko almost

00:01:28.778 --> 00:01:31.700
Just tried to destroy a village of innocent people

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.189
Yeah, he almost went super dark

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:37.012
It also kind helps that they have imagery of all these other fire nation ships in the background

00:01:37.012 --> 00:01:39.014
Like, if you thought Zuko was bad

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.200
Just you wait

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.258
There's that really familiar phrase "Out of the pot and into the frying pan"

00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:46.180
It's pretty applicable given the fire nation overtones and the Agni Kai

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.878
And the fact that Zuko almost does gets cooked in that fight

00:01:48.878 --> 00:01:51.920
Most of you already know that Jason Isaacs is the vioce actor

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.675
Bryan and Mike said that Zhao's character, specifically, was based on

00:01:55.675 --> 00:01:59.895
Jason's villain character, from the Patriot. That's an old Mel Gibson movie

00:01:59.895 --> 00:02:02.937
During that he plays a British imperialist character

00:02:02.937 --> 00:02:05.790
just reaving and raping his way across colonial America

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.940
Most of you probably know him way better as Lucius Malfoy from Harry Potter

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.980
So usually when I talk about Zhao, and Jason Issacs, I talk about Harry Potter stuff

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.000
His character in the Patriot was way worse that Lucius Malfoy

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.754
But that movie is one of the longest movie ever

00:02:19.775 --> 00:02:21.055
It's interminable

00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:22.720
So unless you want to torture yourself

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.329
Just stick with Lucius Malfoy in the Harry Potter films

00:02:25.329 --> 00:02:28.646
So the Zhao-Zuko stuff provides all the dramatic tension

00:02:28.646 --> 00:02:31.015
At least until Aang finds out that all his friends are dead

00:02:31.015 --> 00:02:34.660
For the most part the episode bounces back between the really fun and really dramatic stuff

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.880
Which is one of the reasons why I really like Last Airbender episodes

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.523
They just do a really good job of being both really funny

00:02:40.523 --> 00:02:42.139
And really dramatic at the same time

00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:45.009
Like going back and forth between one and the other seamlessly

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.200
I think the last season of Korra 

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.780
Was way heavier on drama

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.440
So I always walked away from those episodes feeling really emotionally drained

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.635
So, if you want to feel better about yourself

00:02:54.635 --> 00:02:57.564
I think Last Airbender, is a better tea to drink

00:02:57.894 --> 00:03:01.414
Number 3: Zhao explains the Fire Nations' Grand Plan

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:04.578
There's so much going on in this Zuko-Zhao storyline

00:03:04.578 --> 00:03:07.242
But it also serves as this giant info dump

00:03:07.242 --> 00:03:09.091
On the future of the Fire Nations' Plan

00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:11.896
And it shines a light on Zuko's father

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:12.900
Fire Lord Ozai

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.120
It's a good reminder that

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.808
No matter how bad Zhao seems

00:03:15.808 --> 00:03:18.074
He's just following the orders of the Fire Lord

00:03:18.074 --> 00:03:20.319
Or the orders as he interprets them

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:22.135
You get a lot of that with Minions

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.635
They're given specific orders, but then they go off-book

00:03:24.635 --> 00:03:26.474
And that's usually where things go bad

00:03:26.474 --> 00:03:28.846
The big reminder here, I think, is that map

00:03:28.846 --> 00:03:33.218
Does this not remind you of Kuvira staring at the map during Korra last year

00:03:33.218 --> 00:03:35.754
Bryan and Mike have always done a good job at invoking

00:03:35.754 --> 00:03:37.662
Last Airbender imagery in Korra episodes

00:03:37.662 --> 00:03:39.940
So now that we're re-watching the old stuff

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.214
Try to pick out familiar Korra scenes

00:03:42.214 --> 00:03:45.819
That's like one of the biggest things I do when I re-watch big anthology series

00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:46.760
It's really fun

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.900
Usually the first time when you watch something you're more focused on the plot,

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.395
And like what's going on with the characters on the surface level so you miss

00:03:52.395 --> 00:03:54.375
like little background visual details

00:03:54.375 --> 00:03:57.049
Number 2: Aang at the Southern Air Temple

00:03:57.049 --> 00:04:00.544
So they finally arrive, and Aang takes them on the Grand Tour

00:04:00.544 --> 00:04:04.046
The Air-Ball court, nice reminder from Meelo playing with the new airbenders 

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.020
In Korra book 3

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.497
And how they turned that whole back mountain slope into a crazy obstacle course

00:04:08.497 --> 00:04:12.322
I still want to go-I want a vacation at the Southern Air Temple

00:04:12.322 --> 00:04:15.100
Even though now...it's still probably being rebuilt

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.670
Just the idea that Airbenders

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:20.462
Which on the surface, seem like such a zen group of people have a game they would play

00:04:20.536 --> 00:04:21.576
It's so much fun

00:04:21.576 --> 00:04:22.735
Like Aang is a child

00:04:22.735 --> 00:04:24.804
of course he's going to be playing games all of the time

00:04:24.804 --> 00:04:27.400
Sometimes you look at the adult characters and forget that

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.658
Maybe that's why the Korra characters spent less time doing fun stuff

00:04:30.658 --> 00:04:33.303
Just because they're all in their early twenties by the time the series ended 

00:04:33.303 --> 00:04:35.862
And all the Aang team members were way, way, younger

00:04:35.862 --> 00:04:38.510
I'd say, you know, of the Southern Air Temple locations

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:41.327
The Hall of Avatar Statues--Probably my favourite place

00:04:41.327 --> 00:04:43.220
Opening the door here; so much fun

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.204
It actually kind reminds me of Harry Potter

00:04:45.204 --> 00:04:46.656
with the Chamber of Secrets

00:04:46.656 --> 00:04:48.303
Just using magic to open doors

00:04:48.303 --> 00:04:51.180
I guess you could also consider it like opening Dumbledore's door

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.940
See how many times you can say that fast

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.260
"Dumbledore's Door"

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:58.449
At some point, I would like to names and histories for all these Avatars

00:04:58.449 --> 00:05:00.569
We really only know about a handful of them

00:05:00.569 --> 00:05:04.500
I know all of you were wondering, after the Southern Air Temple was destroyed in Legend of Korra

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.799
If there was a Hall of Avatar Statues

00:05:06.799 --> 00:05:08.249
In one of the other Temples

00:05:08.249 --> 00:05:09.140
Like Air Temple Island

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.420
That-that remains to be seen

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:13.578
I do think that there are statues in other temples

00:05:13.578 --> 00:05:16.060
Just taking a step back, I feel that Studio Amir's job

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:18.275
Animating the Southern Air Temple in Legend of Korra

00:05:18.516 --> 00:05:20.116
Did it much more justice

00:05:20.116 --> 00:05:21.826
than the animation on Last Airbender

00:05:21.826 --> 00:05:23.826
Obviously it's a very different animation studio

00:05:23.826 --> 00:05:26.034
So you can't compare quite as much

00:05:26.034 --> 00:05:29.324
And I don't want to judge Last Airbender based on Legend of Korra

00:05:29.324 --> 00:05:33.753
But if you want a really, trippy, beautiful exploration of that place

00:05:33.826 --> 00:05:35.826
Just watch the Book 3 episodes

00:05:35.826 --> 00:05:37.140
Moving on, we meet Momo

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:41.440
His relationship with the winged lemurs is actually a lot like the Sky Bison in Legend of Korra

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.000
Momo's supposed to be the only one to survive the genocide

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.656
But by the time we get to Korra

00:05:45.656 --> 00:05:48.274
Meelo is commanding an army of winged lemurs

00:05:48.274 --> 00:05:51.356
So, somewhere else in the world, there's some thriving colony

00:05:51.356 --> 00:05:54.520
I know a lot of people were confused about the sky bison in Korra

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:55.724
where they all came from

00:05:55.724 --> 00:05:57.288
Bryan and Mike explained that

00:05:57.288 --> 00:05:58.942
this island here, in Book 2

00:05:58.942 --> 00:06:00.469
served as kinda a sanctuary

00:06:00.469 --> 00:06:02.959
where they were bred in seclusion during the 100 year war

00:06:02.959 --> 00:06:05.745
Aang loses his shit and goes into the Avatar state

00:06:05.745 --> 00:06:07.218
when he finds Gyatso's skeleton

00:06:07.218 --> 00:06:10.580
And it hits him that he bailed, when they needed him the most

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.540
It's a nice emotional touchstone for the character

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:13.780
It's a big call to action

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:17.240
Even though all that still did not stop him from still being a little kid

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:19.914
after recommitting himself to training in the other elements

00:06:19.914 --> 00:06:23.949
Like, he's rededicated himself to his purpose but he still finds time to have fun

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:27.800
And, my Number 1 Moment: Zuko vs Zhao in Agni Kai

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.120
So they don't take it as far as you'd think they would

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.680
because it's a Nickelodeon show, I mean, it's for children

00:06:32.688 --> 00:06:36.560
But Agni Kai, always felt to me, like it was meant to be a duel to the death

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.157
Thunder Dome rules: Two people enter, one person leaves

00:06:40.157 --> 00:06:43.555
The way they use it in the series is much more like a non-lethal fight of honour

00:06:43.555 --> 00:06:46.242
But it's still used as a stand in for trial by combat

00:06:46.242 --> 00:06:49.207
Like when one character challenges the word of another

00:06:49.207 --> 00:06:51.479
So, if you were say, accused of something

00:06:51.479 --> 00:06:54.607
you could probably bluff your way into an Agni Kai with your accuser

00:06:54.607 --> 00:06:57.083
And if you won, you might be allowed to walk away

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:59.502
I guess that would depend on the severity of your crime

00:06:59.502 --> 00:07:02.138
Zuko defeating Zhao, is just a nice reminder that

00:07:02.138 --> 00:07:06.117
even though he's this cast away character, he's still very powerful, very important

00:07:06.117 --> 00:07:10.555
It's also a really good example of turning someone who initially, seemed like a really simple villain

00:07:10.555 --> 00:07:12.765
into a much more sympathetic anti-hero

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:14.983
despite the fact that he's still gunning for Aang

00:07:14.983 --> 00:07:17.191
He still has that murder-y look on his face

00:07:17.191 --> 00:07:19.169
Here's my big question for you guys:

00:07:19.169 --> 00:07:20.653
What did you like more in the episode?

00:07:20.653 --> 00:07:21.977
Did you like the Southern Air Temple stuff

00:07:21.977 --> 00:07:23.674
Or did you like Agni Kai better

00:07:23.674 --> 00:07:26.012
I mean, I feel like Agni Kai was where all the action was

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:30.757
But they definitely paid off a lot of the lore of the Southern Air Temple in Legend of Korra

00:07:30.757 --> 00:07:34.135
So here's just some cool behind-the-scenes facts from the episode

00:07:34.135 --> 00:07:37.200
So when the writers were first working on Momo's character

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.540
they thought about presenting him as the reincarnation of Gyatso the Monk

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.395
But they ultimately decided against it

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:47.220
Momo's name actually derives from the Japanese term for peach

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.620
So after Momo steals the fruit from Sokka

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.394
It's like Aang names him based on the fruit

00:07:52.394 --> 00:07:55.870
Then the term Agni Kai is actually Bengali for Fire Quarrel

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:00.622
And Combustion Man's name actually derives from his time in Agni Kai fight

00:08:00.882 --> 00:08:04.322
Like he was so good, so quick, because of his ability

00:08:04.322 --> 00:08:07.274
That they named him Combustion Man because he blew fights up

00:08:07.274 --> 00:08:09.120
Just overall, the episode's great

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.320
I don't have any significant thumbs down

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.680
It's just--an amazing example of a story that

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.831
moves the plot forward in a really big way

00:08:15.831 --> 00:08:18.520
giving us, you know, a really big road map for the series:

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.879
like what's going on with the Fire Nation,

00:08:19.879 --> 00:08:21.560
What Aang's going to be doing;

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.580
It generates a ton of new lore for the series,

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.380
via the Southern Air Temple as well as the Agni Kai stuff

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.744
And it turns the villain--Zuko right here--into an Anti-Hero

